1
00:00:00,311 --> 00:00:03,061
(Howard:)- Next time, make your own date.
- Didn't wanna make this one.

2
00:00:03,231 --> 00:00:06,691
(Leonard:)Look on the bright side, she might
turn out to be a nice, beautiful girl.

3
00:00:06,859 --> 00:00:09,489
Great, we get married,
I won't be able to talk to her...

4
00:00:09,654 --> 00:00:12,654
(Raj:)...and we'll spend the rest of our lives
in total silence.

5
00:00:12,824 --> 00:00:14,404
It worked for my parents.

6
00:00:14,575 --> 00:00:16,115
[KNOCK ON DOOR]

7
00:00:16,285 --> 00:00:17,495
- Hi, guys.
- Oh, hey.

8
00:00:17,662 --> 00:00:18,702
I need guinea pigs.

9
00:00:18,871 --> 00:00:23,331
(Sheldon:)Okay, there's a lab animal supply
company in Reseda you could try.

10
00:00:23,501 --> 00:00:27,291
(Sheldon:)But if your research is going to have
human applications, I suggest white mice.

11
00:00:27,463 --> 00:00:30,503
(Sheldon:)Their brain chemistry
is far closer to ours.

12
00:00:31,717 --> 00:00:35,177
(Penny:)I swear to God, Sheldon, one day,
I'm gonna get the hang of talking to you.

13
00:00:36,305 --> 00:00:38,845
(Leonard:)His mom's been saying that for years.

14
00:00:41,102 --> 00:00:43,522
(Leonard:)- What's up?
- Well, I convinced the restaurant...

15
00:00:43,688 --> 00:00:46,898
...to give me a bartending shift
so I need to practice mixing drinks.

16
00:00:47,066 --> 00:00:51,196
Oh, well, great. The key to acquiring
proficiency in any task is repetition.

17
00:00:51,362 --> 00:00:52,992
(Sheldon:)With certain obvious exceptions.

18
00:00:54,532 --> 00:00:58,022
(Sheldon:)Suicide, for example.

